  "raw_response": "{\n  \"title\": \"EURUSD 15-minute chart illustrating an inducement zone between major high and major low\",\n  \"school\": \"Smart Money Concepts (SMC)\",\n  \"asset\": \"EURUSD\",\n  \"timeframe\": \"15M\",\n  \"market_context\": \"Price was in a downtrend, having formed a major high at 1.08750 and a major low at 1.08500. The analyst identified a minor internal pullback high labeled 'Inducement' just below the major high, serving as a required level to break before a valid BOS.\",\n  \"key_observation\": \"The analyst highlighted a minor internal high (inducement) that price needed to take out before a valid break of structure could occur—acting as a trap for retail traders who enter prematurely.\",\n  \"analysis_steps\": [\n    \"Step 1: Identified the major swing high at 1.08750 and major swing low at 1.08500 on the 15-minute EURUSD chart.\",\n    \"Step 2: Located a minor internal pullback high labeled 'Inducement' just below the major high, which price had to reclaim before a valid bullish break of structure.\",\n    \"Step 3: Noted that price had not yet broken above the inducement level, meaning a true BOS was not yet confirmed despite apparent upward momentum.\"\n  ],\n  \"outcome\": null,\n  \"lessons\": \"Inducement zones act as critical filters: a valid break of structure requires price to first invalidate the inducement (minor swing), preventing premature entries and revealing institutional trapping behavior.\",\n  \"primary_image_frame_id\": \"ueXZlGqlfqY_f002\",\n  \"supporting_image_frame_ids\": [],\n  \"related_concept",
